#H1[Executive summary]
*Overall verdict.* V8.3 is a coherent, well-documented concept design whose *house works*: the guest / family separation, the courtyard heart, the master suite, the maid wing, the fire strategy at home level and the two plumbing clusters all walk through their scenarios. It is *not ready to freeze for V9.0*, for four reasons that have nothing to do with drawing quality: (1) the plot's setback margin is still provisional (V-01, open since V6); (2) nothing structural has been checked by an engineer and there is no soil report (V-02); (3) the owner's 3 Nov decisions left *bedroom 1 and the future kids' bedroom without a shower on their floor* (V-03), a validation failure for this family; (4) the services concept has *no heating and no energy-code envelope* (V-04) and *no water in a power cut* (V-05). The remaining majors are site and yard conflicts created by the latest moves (the parking bay against the north windows V-07, the hood exhaust beside the outdoor counter V-08) and two accepted residual risks the owner should see in writing (the open stair V-09, the undecided suite-bath drainage and the overfull utility room V-10). Of the 37 requirements, 24 are met, 9 partly, 1 not met (R-11), 3 not verifiable yet. Findings: #n-sev("critical") critical · #n-sev("major") major · #n-sev("minor") minor · #n-sev("suggestion") suggestions.

