// ====================================================================================== 3 · consistency
#H1[3 · Verification · consistency across the files]
#text(7.2pt, fill: luma(110))[`tools/check.py` compiles everything, compares the two studies' rooms with the CSVs, the DXFs' areas with the CSVs and rebuilds the 3D with its own checks: every geometric link is machine-checked. The mismatches below are therefore in the *texts and records*, not in the geometry.]
- *Room names and sizes:* `data/rooms_gf.csv` / `rooms_ff.csv` ↔ `guest_wing.typ`, `east_wing.typ`, `ff_family.typ`, `ff_suite.typ` ↔ the DXFs ↔ the 3D: *no mismatch* (check.py sections 3, 4, 6). The presentation's schedules and `PROJECT_V8.md` §3 are generated from the same data.
- *Doors and windows:* the ground-floor doors come from `presentation.typ` (gf-doors), the first-floor ones from the two studies, the heights from `3d/params.yaml`; the 3D flags any height without a door: *none*. One text mismatch: `docs/AIR_SYSTEM.md` described the grille at the old height until V8.3 (corrected in this release).
- *Stair and lift:* `studies/structure.typ` `st` → the 3D (direction-aware) → the fire study: consistent; `studies/stair_flip.typ` still shows the *old* family bath and the pre-flip routes as its record (V-18).
- *Plumbing clusters and stacks:* `studies/plumbing.typ` rounds 1–2 ↔ `ff_family.typ` drains ↔ `guest_wing.typ` ↔ the site plan's chambers: consistent after V8.3; the round-1 scenario B still names the GF shower P1 as data (withdrawn in the text).
- *Roof ↔ plumbing:* the roof reserves a *water tank zone* (R10–R3); the plumbing study's water scheme has *no roof tank* (V-05): a concept mismatch to decide.
- *Site plan ↔ plans ↔ 3D:* the counter, the grill, the screen, the gas, the bins and the paths are the same numbers in `site_plan.typ`, `design_gf.typ` and `3d/character.yaml` (checked by hand at V8.3); the site plan's parking bay vs the north windows (V-07) and the hood vs the counter (V-08) are *design* conflicts the checks did not cover.
- *Open items:* `data/open_items.csv` ↔ `OPEN_ITEMS.md` ↔ the presentation sheet 10: numbered in the same order (checked); the review status rows updated for V8.3.
- *Decisions log:* 57 rows; the V8.1-labelled rows mix the tower removal (V8.1) with items applied in V8.2 (relabelled at V8.2) — a labelling, not a content, mismatch (V-18).
- *Record studies that no longer describe the house:* `stair_flip.typ` (the family bath), `south_wing.typ` (the stair tower and the stair room in its sections), `gf_shower.typ` (closed), `bedroom1_bath.typ` pages 1–2 (option A as adopted, now reopened), `air_system.typ` ("the benches" in one table head): each carries a header note; none has a page-1 banner (V-18).
#ar[*الاتساق:* الروابط الهندسية بين الملفات تُفحص آليا ولا تعارض فيها؛ التعارضات الموجودة في النصوص والسجلات القديمة (دراسة قلب الدرج، دراسة الجناح الجنوبي، دش الأرضي، خزان السطح بين دراسة السطح ودراسة السباكة) وفي قرارات التصميم الأخيرة (الموقف أمام النوافذ الشمالية، مخرج الشفاط بجوار المطبخ الخارجي).]

