#H1[6 · Comparison with the V6 review (30 Oct 2026)]
- *Resolved since V6:* the three criticals are two-thirds closed: Y-01 (the courtyard envelope: W1 / W2 / W3, V7.0) and A-01 (the lift at construction, V6.3); S-03 (the setback) is *still open* (V-01). Of the 27 majors, 20 are resolved on the files (the TV wall, the maid room, the gallery width, the door widths, the courtyard layout and its safety, the air system, the fire strategy, the roof access, the office, the site plan's parking, guest approach, garden, yard, PV, generator, security, the food route, the ground-floor bathrooms by decision), 6 partly (G-02 daylight, G-03 MEP, T-01 structure, E-02 / E-03 MEP and plumbing, S-08 the septic and tanks), 2 open (T-03 soil, E-07 acoustics).
- *What improved most:* the house became closable and filterable (R-25), the roofline and the roof access were simplified, the site is planned, the plumbing has a strategy, every bedroom but one has its own bathroom, the courtyard is level and furnished.
- *What is new since V6 (not in that review):* the heating / energy gap (V-04: the V6 review flagged the open envelope, not the missing heating); the power-cut water (V-05, created by removing the generator); bedroom 1's shower (V-03, created by the 3 Nov split); the north parking bay against the windows (V-07) and the hood beside the outdoor counter (V-08), both created by the site decisions; the septic outside the wall (V-06, the owner's information); the record-keeping drift (V-18).
- *Severity trend:* V6 had 3 critical / 27 major / 25 minor-suggestion findings; this interim review has #n-sev("critical") critical / #n-sev("major") major / #n-sev("minor") minor / #n-sev("suggestion") suggestions. The two criticals are the same two unresolved external dependencies (the survey, the engineer); the majors are fewer and more specific.
